text:
JWT `exp` in seconds. `Date.now()` in milliseconds.

**Bug:**
```js
if (Date.now() > payload.exp) // wrong — always false, exp looks huge
```

**Fix:**
```js
if (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > payload.exp) // correct
```

Or:
```js
if (Date.now() > payload.exp * 1000) // also correct
```

**Full middleware:**
```js
function authMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'No token' });

  try {
    const payload = jwt.verify(token, SECRET); // verify() checks exp automatically
    req.user = payload;
    next();
  } catch (err) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: err.message });
  }
}
```

Better fix: let `jwt.verify()` handle expiry check — throws `TokenExpiredError` if expired. No manual `Date.now()` needed.
